Mistakes I have done
Corrections in your code
1. Comparing an index with a value
You wrote:
minQueue.peekLast() > nums[right]
minQueue.peekLast() returns an index. You need the value at that index:
nums[minQueue.peekLast()] > nums[right]
The same correction applies to maxQueue:
nums[maxQueue.peekLast()] < nums[right]
2. Maximum and minimum are at the front
You wrote:
maxQueue.peekLast() - minQueue.peekLast()
These are indices, not the maximum and minimum values.
Use:
nums[maxQueue.peekFirst()] - nums[minQueue.peekFirst()]
The queue fronts contain the current maximum and minimum.
3. Compare with left, not right
When shrinking, the element leaving the window is nums[left].
You wrote:
if (maxQueue.peekFirst() == right)
It should be:
if (maxQueue.peekFirst() == left)
4. Remove from the correct queue
You wrote:
if (minQueue.peekFirst() == right)
    maxQueue.pollFirst();
It should remove from minQueue:
if (minQueue.peekFirst() == left) {
    minQueue.pollFirst();
}

1. Use peekFirst() to get the maximum and minimum
You wrote:
nums[maxQueue.peekLast()] - nums[minQueue.peekLast()]
The maximum and minimum are stored at the front:
nums[maxQueue.peekFirst()] - nums[minQueue.peekFirst()]
2. Remove from minQueue, not maxQueue
